Opt-in per-message traffic census (busd::stats).

MUST apply after unique-activation.patch ("w" sorts last).

Off by default; free when off. `touch $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/busd-stats.on` turns
it on (checked every 5 s); while the file exists busd rewrites
`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/busd-stats` every 5 s with the messages it routed in that
period: one line per (type, sender, destination, interface.member) with the
message count and the number of deliveries it cost (a broadcast signal is
sent to every connection whose match rules accept it). Senders are unique
names; ask the bus (GetConnectionUnixProcessID) to map them to processes.
Written for lane/mediabus (2026-10-17) to answer
"is the session bus storming during media playback" from inside a running
session without restarting it.


